{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA 344-bug corpus analysis (session log 5eb0-52a3-45f0-43e5) identified recurring escape channels: surface-parity gaps, contention semantics missed at authoring time, inert/miswired config, wall-clock flakes, unlocked store writes, auto-filer breakage, prose-only provenance rotting in code comments, and bug fixes landing without plan review. Each child was individually design-reviewed and approved by the operator (decision table in the session log; per-change experiments under /tmp/exp*.py referenced in child descriptions).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Bug provenance is observable at creation (detected-by) and trend-queryable (bug_trends metrics lens), without new required user input.\n- [x] Deterministic pre-LLM gates exist for: raw git writes bypassing the store seam, unread config schema fields, upper-bound wall-clock asserts in tests, unchecked AC checkboxes at close, historical-context rot in code comments, and oversized bug-fix diffs lacking a current plan-review attestation.\n- [x] The reconciler transport is typed end-to-end, declared field asymmetries are pinned by property tests, and pagination loops are deduplicated into shared iterators.\n- [x] Production shell logic (reconcile-bridge/canary workflow bodies, probe harness, vote normalizer) is migrated to Python per the strangler-fig policy.\n- [x] Canary/automation bug filing follows the hardened dedup pattern and a documented bug-creation contract.\n- [x] Engine-layer validation placement is advisory-enforced at plan review.\n- [x] rebar-debug and rebar-implement skills (and the shared test-design standard) encode the approved discipline upgrades: ticket writebacks, two-axis invariant sweeps, surface census, config-effect contrast, case-(c) contention triggers, gate-finding oracle upgrades, and residual-gap disposition.\n- [x] Explicit review-plan on a bug runs a real review, and the Gerrit backstop blocks oversized bug fixes lacking one.\n- [x] Code comments citing dead SHAs/run-ids/dates are remediated to ticket citations, with a CI guard preventing regression."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785810167586771001,"uuid":"b2a5cc6a-3c2b-49c0-b23f-cfe2d00a50bf"}